{"body":"## Accepted result and scope\n\nThe Röver–Sapir Question111 about finitely presented subgroups of Thompson F remains **unsolved,5/5**. The credited wreath/FP2 obstruction and embedded non-FP2 torsion examples; simple-derived subdirect/normalizer torsion-freeness; solvable PL-image torsion-freeness for the original FP2 domain; ordinarily finitely generated ambient-normal subgroup germ detection; and finite-piece PL unique-root/balanced-power obstructions and nonembedding nilpotent proxy examples. These are scoped partial results; the required general isolated-commutator conclusion or an embedded finitely presented torsion counterexample remains absent.\n\n## Correction and adversarial evidence\n\nThe unsupported historical diagram-group assertion is superseded by an explicit current scope note: the packet proves neither a universal membership reduction nor a finitely presented non-diagram subgroup counterexample. Two additive correction files and all three current wrappers bind this repair;41 historical target paths are unchanged.\n\nRoot reconstructed all five proofs, read executable sources and primary hypotheses, reproduced562635 author and110736 historical assertions, and checked three distinct initial families. A first whole-package adversary identified the wording repair. A new corrected-head reviewer found no further required repair; root reproduced its ten complete candidate/control streams byte exactly, verified47 Git objects,111 nested bindings,37 bounded outputs and both independent seals, including81628 new post-candidate assertions.\n\nSeven fresh complete primary PDFs match historical bindings. Thirteen historical processed text/PNG bindings remain unreproduced; source-free public verification checks0/20 optional raw bindings. The accessible credited splitting dependency is BGK, not a newly retrieved Bieri–Strebel proof. No present worldwide open-status or priority certification is claimed.\n\n[Acceptance decision](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr381_30003853/ACCEPTANCE_DECISION.md); [fresh corrected-head adversary](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr381_30003853/clean_final_adversary/REPORT.md). Original head5b7bd8db9f34294d10862fed0f723055da864df6; accepted corrected head83862044e1bb334d582b2082bf8b63c6b0eee4c5. Queue repair preserves every unrelated row.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in research, drafting, verification and adversarial review. This is unrefereed work and is not external human peer review. Accept as scoped partial progress; no paper, Zenodo deposit, DOI, tracker row or release.\n","headRefOid":"83862044e1bb334d582b2082bf8b63c6b0eee4c5","isDraft":false,"mergeCommit":null,"mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","mergedAt":null,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/381"}
